00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.932
- Lewis asks "Where would
you start in building

00:02:07.932 --> 00:02:12.048
a digital team within a
traditional TV or print agency?"

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.932
- Lewis there's an interesting
thing that I believe in very

00:02:14.932 --> 00:02:19.219
much which is you are what
your actions show you are.

00:02:19.219 --> 00:02:22.273
It's very similar, I'm probably
affected by Bill Parcells,

00:02:22.273 --> 00:02:24.952
in football legendary hall
of famer coach Bill Parcells

00:02:24.952 --> 00:02:27.448
former Jet coach always said
you are what your record

00:02:27.448 --> 00:02:30.018
says you are because everyone's
like we're eight and eight

00:02:30.018 --> 00:02:32.355
but we could have been 10
and six if we you know,

00:02:32.355 --> 00:02:33.615
but at the end of the
day you are what you are.

00:02:33.615 --> 00:02:34.926
Thanks Mike.

00:02:38.406 --> 00:02:41.553
It's very easy to create
a digital practice within

00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:45.365
a traditional print or direct
mail, outdoor media or PR.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.275
All these agencies now have
to shift into the world

00:02:48.275 --> 00:02:49.786
that we've created because
that's where the dollars

00:02:49.786 --> 00:02:53.988
and the momentum and where
the story telling is going.

00:02:53.988 --> 00:02:56.730
This video will be consumed
a hell of a lot more

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.690
in YouTube and Facebook
native than it will

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.675
as a pre roll pop up somewhere.

00:03:02.675 --> 00:03:06.904
And so I think it's super
important that you understand

00:03:06.904 --> 00:03:09.130
you are what your actions say you are.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:12.833
Meaning it's very easy, go out
and hire seven to 12 people

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:16.628
that work in digital social,
bring them into your department

00:03:16.628 --> 00:03:18.480
and now you have that capability.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.864
Now the key for the CEO or
the chairman of the board,

00:03:20.864 --> 00:03:24.192
her and his job is to
really integrate that new,

00:03:24.192 --> 00:03:26.828
we're going through it now
VaynerMedia has a new live

00:03:26.828 --> 00:03:30.517
division called VaynerLive,
it's live events activation.

00:03:30.517 --> 00:03:32.022
It's not what we've historically done.

00:03:32.022 --> 00:03:33.994
It's activating at Coachella or South By

00:03:33.994 --> 00:03:35.275
or things of that nature.

00:03:35.275 --> 00:03:37.905
And we're six months in and
we still have to integrate it

00:03:37.905 --> 00:03:40.119
into the business but we brought in Robert

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.089
and other people that have
done that work in the past.

00:03:42.089 --> 00:03:43.415
Now we have the skill set.

00:03:43.415 --> 00:03:45.268
Now how does that practice mold in

00:03:45.268 --> 00:03:46.534
to the whole organization?

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:49.504
That's the tricky part, that's
where dictatorship comes in.

00:03:49.504 --> 00:03:51.091
That's where letting things happen

00:03:51.091 --> 00:03:52.682
the way they have to happen.

00:03:52.682 --> 00:03:56.113
I'm a big fan of letting things
lie so I've stayed hands-off

00:03:56.113 --> 00:03:57.995
for the first several
six and a half months.

00:03:57.995 --> 00:03:59.220
Now maybe I feel like maybe
like I'll get my hands

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.247
in a little bit dirtier
just get it molded in.

00:04:02.247 --> 00:04:05.280
Leadership is knowing when to
listen, knowing when to talk.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:06.705
Knowing when to take a
step back, knowing when

00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:08.440
to jump in and integrate it.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.483
But the commodity of
hiring people that have

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.993
the skill set to do the
work, it's out there.

00:04:12.993 --> 00:04:15.793
It's just making the
leap to decide to do it.

